{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0114rz7uxSTsq4ekvorAW33W","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tservices:\n2\t  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3\t  # WireGuard peer for the AWS mail edge (34.194.247.228).\n4\t  #\n5\t  # This container OWNS the network namespace that `mailserver` runs inside\n6\t  # (see `network_mode: service:mail-edge-wg` below). Consequences:\n7\t  #   * wg0 / 10.77.0.2 exists inside that netns, so Postfix + Dovecot bind the\n8\t  #     tunnel address directly. No host port publishing, so no EADDRINUSE\n9\t  #     against Traefik, which still holds 0.0.0.0:{25,465,587,993}.\n10\t  #   * No host root required (there is no passwordless sudo on this host, so a\n11\t  #     host-level `wg-quick@wg0` unit is not installable autonomously).\n12\t  #   * Restarting THIS container destroys the netns. `mailserver` MUST be\n13\t  #     restarted afterwards - Docker will not do it for you.\n14\t  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n15\t  mail-edge-wg:\n16\t    image: lscr.io/linuxserver/wireguard:1.0.20260223-r0-ls118\n17\t    container_name: mail-edge-wg\n18\t    restart: unless-stopped\n19\t    cap_add:\n20\t      - NET_ADMIN\n21\t    sysctls:\n22\t      - net.ipv4.conf.all.src_valid_mark=1\n23\t    environment:\n24\t      - PUID=1000\n25\t      - PGID=1000\n26\t      - TZ=America/New_York\n27\t    volumes:\n28\t      # Home peer config, generated by aws/mail-edge. Mode 600, never committed.\n29\t      - /home/administrator/projects/secrets/mail-edge-wg.conf:/config/wg_confs/wg0.conf:ro\n30\t    healthcheck:\n31\t      test: [\"CMD-SHELL\", \"wg show wg0 >/dev/null 2>&1 && ping -c1 -W2 10.77.0.1 >/dev/null 2>&1\"]\n32\t      interval: 30s\n33\t      timeout: 10s\n34\t      retries: 3\n35\t      start_period: 20s\n36\t    networks:\n37\t      # Egress to reach the edge endpoint, plus reachability for postfixadmin.\n38\t      - mailserver-net\n39\t\n40\t  mailserver:\n41\t    image: ghcr.io/docker-mailserver/docker-mailserver:latest\n42\t    container_name: mailserver\n43\t    # `hostname:` is illegal alongside network_mode: service:* (Docker rejects it).\n44\t    # DMS's supported equivalent is OVERRIDE_HOSTNAME, set below.\n45\t    restart: unless-stopped\n46\t    stop_grace_period: 1m\n47\t    # Shares the WireGuard netns. NOTE: no `networks:`, no `ports:`, no Traefik\n48\t    # labels are permitted on a service using network_mode: service:*.\n49\t    network_mode: \"service:mail-edge-wg\"\n50\t    depends_on:\n51\t      mail-edge-wg:\n52\t        condition: service_healthy\n53\t    healthcheck:\n54\t      # Asserts BOTH that Postfix is listening AND that the inherited netns still\n55\t      # has a live wg0. Without the wg0 clause this container reports healthy\n56\t      # while being completely network-dead: restarting mail-edge-wg destroys the\n57\t      # namespace, but Postfix keeps listening inside the orphaned one, so the\n58\t      # port check alone still passes. Verified 2026-07-28.\n59\t      test: [\"CMD-SHELL\", \"ss --listening --ipv4 --tcp | grep --silent ':smtp' && ip link show wg0 >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 1\"]\n60\t      interval: 30s\n61\t      timeout: 10s\n62\t      retries: 3\n63\t    env_file: /home/administrator/projects/secrets/docker-mailserver.env\n64\t    environment:\n65\t      - OVERRIDE_HOSTNAME=mail.ai-servicers.com\n66\t    volumes:\n67\t      - /home/administrator/projects/data/docker-mailserver/mail:/var/mail\n68\t      - /home/administrator/projects/data/docker-mailserver/state:/var/mail-state\n69\t      - ./config:/tmp/docker-mailserver\n70\t      - /home/administrator/projects/data/traefik-certs/ai-servicers.com:/certs:ro\n71\t      - /etc/localtime:/etc/localtime:ro\n72\t    cap_add:\n73\t      - NET_ADMIN\n74\t\n75\t  postfixadmin:\n76\t    image: postfixadmin/postfixadmin:latest\n77\t    container_name: postfixadmin\n78\t    restart: unless-stopped\n79\t    profiles: [\"postfixadmin\"]   # not part of the default stack; DMS uses ACCOUNT_PROVISIONER=FILE\n80\t    environment:\n81\t      - POSTFIXADMIN_DB_TYPE=sqlite\n82\t      - POSTFIXADMIN_SETUP_PASSWORD=${POSTFIXADMIN_SETUP_PASSWORD:-changeme123}\n83\t      # mailserver has no DNS name of its own - it lives in mail-edge-wg's netns.\n84\t      - POSTFIXADMIN_SMTP_SERVER=mail-edge-wg\n85\t      - POSTFIXADMIN_SMTP_PORT=25\n86\t      - POSTFIXADMIN_ENCRYPT=dovecot:BLF-CRYPT\n87\t      - POSTFIXADMIN_DOMAIN=ai-servicers.com\n88\t    volumes:\n89\t      - /home/administrator/projects/data/docker-mailserver/postfixadmin:/var/lib/postfixadmin\n90\t    networks:\n91\t      - mailserver-net\n92\t      - traefik-net\n93\t    labels:\n94\t      - \"traefik.enable=true\"\n95\t      - \"traefik.http.routers.postfixadmin.rule=Host(`postfixadmin.ai-servicers.com`)\"\n96\t      - \"traefik.http.routers.postfixadmin.entrypoints=websecure\"\n97\t      - \"traefik.http.routers.postfixadmin.tls=true\"\n98\t      - \"traefik.http.routers.postfixadmin.tls.certresolver=letsencrypt\"\n99\t      - \"traefik.http.services.postfixadmin.loadbalancer.server.port=80\"\n100\t      - \"traefik.http.routers.postfixadmin.middlewares=auth@docker\"\n101\t\n102\tnetworks:\n103\t  mailserver-net:\n104\t    external: true\n105\t  traefik-net:\n106\t    external: true\n107\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4887fea5-78a1-4b14-a071-ae362ca71a13","uuid":"e9925461-f6dc-4294-8045-4831e3e597ac","timestamp":"2026-07-28T13:53:15.138Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/docker-compose.yml","content":"services:\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # WireGuard peer for the AWS mail edge (34.194.247.228).\n  #\n  # This container OWNS the network namespace that `mailserver` runs inside\n  # (see `network_mode: service:mail-edge-wg` below). Consequences:\n  #   * wg0 / 10.77.0.2 exists inside that netns, so Postfix + Dovecot bind the\n  #     tunnel address directly. No host port publishing, so no EADDRINUSE\n  #     against Traefik, which still holds 0.0.0.0:{25,465,587,993}.\n  #   * No host root required (there is no passwordless sudo on this host, so a\n  #     host-level `wg-quick@wg0` unit is not installable autonomously).\n  #   * Restarting THIS container destroys the netns. `mailserver` MUST be\n  #     restarted afterwards - Docker will not do it for you.\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  mail-edge-wg:\n    image: lscr.io/linuxserver/wireguard:1.0.20260223-r0-ls118\n    container_name: mail-edge-wg\n    restart: unless-stopped\n    cap_add:\n      - NET_ADMIN\n    sysctls:\n      - net.ipv4.conf.all.src_valid_mark=1\n    environment:\n      - PUID=1000\n      - PGID=1000\n      - TZ=America/New_York\n    volumes:\n      # Home peer config, generated by aws/mail-edge. Mode 600, never committed.\n      - /home/administrator/projects/secrets/mail-edge-wg.conf:/config/wg_confs/wg0.conf:ro\n    healthcheck:\n      test: [\"CMD-SHELL\", \"wg show wg0 >/dev/null 2>&1 && ping -c1 -W2 10.77.0.1 >/dev/null 2>&1\"]\n      interval: 30s\n      timeout: 10s\n      retries: 3\n      start_period: 20s\n    networks:\n      # Egress to reach the edge endpoint, plus reachability for postfixadmin.\n      - mailserver-net\n\n  mailserver:\n    image: ghcr.io/docker-mailserver/docker-mailserver:latest\n    container_name: mailserver\n    # `hostname:` is illegal alongside network_mode: service:* (Docker rejects it).\n    # DMS's supported equivalent is OVERRIDE_HOSTNAME, set below.\n    restart: unless-stopped\n    stop_grace_period: 1m\n    # Shares the WireGuard netns. NOTE: no `networks:`, no `ports:`, no Traefik\n    # labels are permitted on a service using network_mode: service:*.\n    network_mode: \"service:mail-edge-wg\"\n    depends_on:\n      mail-edge-wg:\n        condition: service_healthy\n    healthcheck:\n      # Asserts BOTH that Postfix is listening AND that the inherited netns still\n      # has a live wg0. Without the wg0 clause this container reports healthy\n      # while being completely network-dead: restarting mail-edge-wg destroys the\n      # namespace, but Postfix keeps listening inside the orphaned one, so the\n      # port check alone still passes. Verified 2026-07-28.\n      test: [\"CMD-SHELL\", \"ss --listening --ipv4 --tcp | grep --silent ':smtp' && ip link show wg0 >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 1\"]\n      interval: 30s\n      timeout: 10s\n      retries: 3\n    env_file: /home/administrator/projects/secrets/docker-mailserver.env\n    environment:\n      - OVERRIDE_HOSTNAME=mail.ai-servicers.com\n    volumes:\n      - /home/administrator/projects/data/docker-mailserver/mail:/var/mail\n      - /home/administrator/projects/data/docker-mailserver/state:/var/mail-state\n      - ./config:/tmp/docker-mailserver\n      - /home/administrator/projects/data/traefik-certs/ai-servicers.com:/certs:ro\n      - /etc/localtime:/etc/localtime:ro\n    cap_add:\n      - NET_ADMIN\n\n  postfixadmin:\n    image: postfixadmin/postfixadmin:latest\n    container_name: postfixadmin\n    restart: unless-stopped\n    profiles: [\"postfixadmin\"]   # not part of the default stack; DMS uses ACCOUNT_PROVISIONER=FILE\n    environment:\n      - POSTFIXADMIN_DB_TYPE=sqlite\n      - POSTFIXADMIN_SETUP_PASSWORD=${POSTFIXADMIN_SETUP_PASSWORD:-changeme123}\n      # mailserver has no DNS name of its own - it lives in mail-edge-wg's netns.\n      - POSTFIXADMIN_SMTP_SERVER=mail-edge-wg\n      - POSTFIXADMIN_SMTP_PORT=25\n      - POSTFIXADMIN_ENCRYPT=dovecot:BLF-CRYPT\n      - POSTFIXADMIN_DOMAIN=ai-servicers.com\n    volumes:\n      - /home/administrator/projects/data/docker-mailserver/postfixadmin:/var/lib/postfixadmin\n    networks:\n      - mailserver-net\n      - traefik-net\n    labels:\n      - \"traefik.enable=true\"\n      - \"traefik.http.routers.postfixadmin.rule=Host(`postfixadmin.ai-servicers.com`)\"\n      - \"traefik.http.routers.postfixadmin.entrypoints=websecure\"\n      - \"traefik.http.routers.postfixadmin.tls=true\"\n      - \"traefik.http.routers.postfixadmin.tls.certresolver=letsencrypt\"\n      - \"traefik.http.services.postfixadmin.loadbalancer.server.port=80\"\n      - \"traefik.http.routers.postfixadmin.middlewares=auth@docker\"\n\nnetworks:\n  mailserver-net:\n    external: true\n  traefik-net:\n    external: true\n","numLines":107,"startLine":1,"totalLines":107}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdUZqpHTBPPzViYpWP1cW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HRN8Kvv8mBQCdF18oaKJae","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/docs/aws-edge-integration.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":658,"cache_read_input_tokens":59234,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":658},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4887fea5-78a1-4b14-a071-ae362ca71a13","uuid":"b8ed3e17-a4d7-4529-876f-198e4ff37bc8","timestamp":"2026-07-28T13:53:15.439Z","request_id":"req_011CdUZqnXnMqGzP7qnqXNRR"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HRN8Kvv8mBQCdF18oaKJae","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Running behind the AWS mail-edge\n2\t\n3\tHow this `docker-mailserver` (DMS) stack works when its public ports are terminated on an\n4\tAWS edge and tunnelled home, instead of being exposed directly. The **AWS half** lives in\n5\t[`~/projects/aws/mail-edge/README.md`](/home/administrator/projects/aws/mail-edge/README.md);\n6\tread both — they are one system.\n7\t\n8\t## Why this is needed\n9\t\n10\tHome is on **Verizon residential**: inbound 25 is blocked, the IP is dynamic, and it's on the\n11\tSpamhaus PBL so outbound mail is rejected. The AWS edge gives us a public Elastic IP with\n12\treverse DNS. DMS stays the **single source of truth** for all mail config; AWS is a dumb pipe.\n13\t\n14\t## The one thing that must change here: PROXY protocol\n15\t\n16\tIf the edge just TCP-forwards, DMS would see **every** connection as coming from the edge's\n17\ttunnel IP — breaking Rspamd scoring, greylisting, and Fail2ban (they'd all act on one IP).\n18\tThe fix is **PROXY protocol**: HAProxy on the edge prepends the real client IP, and DMS is\n19\tconfigured to trust and read it. Postfix and Dovecot both support it. [DMS tutorial][dmsproxy]\n20\t\n21\t> ⚠️ **Verify exact directives against the current DMS tutorial before applying** — DMS is on\n22\t> v15.x and the override filenames/port numbers below track the *edge/latest* \"Mail Server\n23\t> behind a Proxy\" doc. There's also an open request to make this env-var-driven ([#3866][iss]),\n24\t> so a newer DMS may simplify it. Treat the shapes below as the design, not copy-paste.\n25\t\n26\t### Postfix — `config/postfix-main.cf` + `config/postfix-master.cf`\n27\t\n28\t- Port 25 goes through `postscreen`, so enable proxy protocol there:\n29\t  - `postfix-main.cf`: `postscreen_upstream_proxy_protocol = haproxy`\n30\t  - `postfix-master.cf`: `smtp/inet/postscreen_upstream_proxy_protocol=haproxy`\n31\t- Submission/SMTPS read it directly:\n32\t  - `submission/inet/smtpd_upstream_proxy_protocol=haproxy`\n33\t  - `smtps/inet/smtpd_upstream_proxy_protocol=haproxy`\n34\t\n35\t### Dovecot — `config/dovecot.cf`\n36\t\n37\t- `haproxy_trusted_networks = <edge WireGuard tunnel IP>` (trust ONLY the tunnel peer)\n38\t- `haproxy_timeout = 3 secs`\n39\t- Add PROXY-protocol `inet_listener`s on the dedicated ports the edge targets\n40\t  (tutorial uses `10143` for imap, `10993` for imaps) with `haproxy = yes`.\n41\t\n42\t### The contract with the edge\n43\t\n44\t| Public port (edge) | → home listener | PROXY variant |\n45\t|---|---|---|\n46\t| 25 (postscreen) | `10025` (or as tutorial defines) | `send-proxy` (v1) |\n47\t| 587 submission | `10587` | `send-proxy` |\n48\t| 465 smtps | `10465` | `send-proxy` |\n49\t| 993 imaps | `10993` | `send-proxy-v2` |\n50\t| 143 imap | `10143` | `send-proxy-v2` |\n51\t\n52\tHAProxy uses `send-proxy` for Postfix backends and `send-proxy-v2` for Dovecot. Keep these\n53\tport numbers in lockstep with `aws/mail-edge` HAProxy config — they are the seam.\n54\t\n55\t## Network / tunnel\n56\t\n57\t- Home runs a **WireGuard** peer dialling out to the edge (outbound UDP 51820 is not\n58\t  ISP-blocked). `PersistentKeepalive = 25` so the NAT mapping stays open.\n59\t- DMS's proxy-protocol listeners only need to be reachable **from the tunnel**, not the LAN or\n60\t  internet. Bind/firewall accordingly.\n61\t- `haproxy_trusted_networks` (Dovecot) and Postfix's implicit trust must name the **edge's\n62\t  tunnel IP** — if that's wrong, PROXY headers are ignored or spoofable.\n63\t\n64\t## DNS (public `ai-servicers.com`)\n65\t\n66\t| Record | Value | Notes |\n67\t|---|---|---|\n68\t| MX | `mail.ai-servicers.com` pri 10 | receivers connect here → Elastic IP |\n69\t| `mail` A | Elastic IP | set in `aws/mail-edge` |\n70\t| PTR | `mail.ai-servicers.com` | **AWS-side**, via the port-25 form — not ours to set |\n71\t| SPF | `v=spf1 mx -all` (or `ip4:<EIP> -all`) | authorise the edge IP as sender |\n72\t| DKIM | generated by DMS (`setup config dkim`) | publish the TXT it emits |\n73\t| DMARC | `v=DMARC1; p=quarantine; rua=mailto:postmaster@ai-servicers.com` | start at `p=none` to monitor |\n74\t\n75\t## Accounts\n76\t\n77\tMailboxes/domains via **postfixadmin** (already in the compose) or `setup email add`. Nothing\n78\tabout account management changes under the edge.\n79\t\n80\t## Test plan (before trusting it)\n81\t\n82\t1. **Tunnel up:** `wg show` both ends; ping tunnel IPs.\n83\t2. **Receive:** from an external account, mail to a test mailbox; confirm delivery.\n84\t3. **Real IP preserved:** check `Received:` headers + Rspamd logs show the *sender's* IP, not\n85\t   the edge tunnel IP. This is the whole point — if it shows the tunnel IP, PROXY protocol is\n86\t   misconfigured.\n87\t4. **Send:** `swaks --to you@gmail.com --from test@ai-servicers.com --server <tunnel>` ; confirm\n88\t   it leaves via the edge (outbound 25 must be unblocked first) and lands in inbox, not spam.\n89\t5. **Deliverability:** mail-tester.com / check SPF+DKIM+DMARC all pass, PTR matches (`dig -x`).\n90\t6. **Fail2ban:** confirm it bans on the real client IP, not the tunnel.\n91\t\n92\t## Current stack state (2026-07-09)\n93\t\n94\t- `mailserver` + `postfixadmin` containers are **defined but not running** (not in `docker ps -a`).\n95\t- Traefik currently holds 25/465/587/993 on the host. Under this design those move to the AWS\n96\t  edge / WireGuard path — **decide** whether Traefik keeps any mail port locally or steps out.\n97\t- No PROXY-protocol config present yet.\n98\t\n99\t## Sources\n100\t\n101\t- [Docker Mailserver — Mail Server behind a Proxy][dmsproxy]\n102\t- [DMS issue #3866 — PROXY protocol via env (future simplification)][iss]\n103\t\n104\t[dmsproxy]: https://docker-mailserver.github.io/docker-mailserver/edge/examples/tutorials/mailserver-behind-proxy/\n105\t[iss]: https://github.com/docker-mailserver/docker-mailserver/issues/3866\n106\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4887fea5-78a1-4b14-a071-ae362ca71a13","uuid":"952591c9-e950-449a-b038-83446756729b","timestamp":"2026-07-28T13:53:15.444Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/docs/aws-edge-integration.md","content":"# Running behind the AWS mail-edge\n\nHow this `docker-mailserver` (DMS) stack works when its public ports are terminated on an\nAWS edge and tunnelled home, instead of being exposed directly. The **AWS half** lives in\n[`~/projects/aws/mail-edge/README.md`](/home/administrator/projects/aws/mail-edge/README.md);\nread both — they are one system.\n\n## Why this is needed\n\nHome is on **Verizon residential**: inbound 25 is blocked, the IP is dynamic, and it's on the\nSpamhaus PBL so outbound mail is rejected. The AWS edge gives us a public Elastic IP with\nreverse DNS. DMS stays the **single source of truth** for all mail config; AWS is a dumb pipe.\n\n## The one thing that must change here: PROXY protocol\n\nIf the edge just TCP-forwards, DMS would see **every** connection as coming from the edge's\ntunnel IP — breaking Rspamd scoring, greylisting, and Fail2ban (they'd all act on one IP).\nThe fix is **PROXY protocol**: HAProxy on the edge prepends the real client IP, and DMS is\nconfigured to trust and read it. Postfix and Dovecot both support it. [DMS tutorial][dmsproxy]\n\n> ⚠️ **Verify exact directives against the current DMS tutorial before applying** — DMS is on\n> v15.x and the override filenames/port numbers below track the *edge/latest* \"Mail Server\n> behind a Proxy\" doc. There's also an open request to make this env-var-driven ([#3866][iss]),\n> so a newer DMS may simplify it. Treat the shapes below as the design, not copy-paste.\n\n### Postfix — `config/postfix-main.cf` + `config/postfix-master.cf`\n\n- Port 25 goes through `postscreen`, so enable proxy protocol there:\n  - `postfix-main.cf`: `postscreen_upstream_proxy_protocol = haproxy`\n  - `postfix-master.cf`: `smtp/inet/postscreen_upstream_proxy_protocol=haproxy`\n- Submission/SMTPS read it directly:\n  - `submission/inet/smtpd_upstream_proxy_protocol=haproxy`\n  - `smtps/inet/smtpd_upstream_proxy_protocol=haproxy`\n\n### Dovecot — `config/dovecot.cf`\n\n- `haproxy_trusted_networks = <edge WireGuard tunnel IP>` (trust ONLY the tunnel peer)\n- `haproxy_timeout = 3 secs`\n- Add PROXY-protocol `inet_listener`s on the dedicated ports the edge targets\n  (tutorial uses `10143` for imap, `10993` for imaps) with `haproxy = yes`.\n\n### The contract with the edge\n\n| Public port (edge) | → home listener | PROXY variant |\n|---|---|---|\n| 25 (postscreen) | `10025` (or as tutorial defines) | `send-proxy` (v1) |\n| 587 submission | `10587` | `send-proxy` |\n| 465 smtps | `10465` | `send-proxy` |\n| 993 imaps | `10993` | `send-proxy-v2` |\n| 143 imap | `10143` | `send-proxy-v2` |\n\nHAProxy uses `send-proxy` for Postfix backends and `send-proxy-v2` for Dovecot. Keep these\nport numbers in lockstep with `aws/mail-edge` HAProxy config — they are the seam.\n\n## Network / tunnel\n\n- Home runs a **WireGuard** peer dialling out to the edge (outbound UDP 51820 is not\n  ISP-blocked). `PersistentKeepalive = 25` so the NAT mapping stays open.\n- DMS's proxy-protocol listeners only need to be reachable **from the tunnel**, not the LAN or\n  internet. Bind/firewall accordingly.\n- `haproxy_trusted_networks` (Dovecot) and Postfix's implicit trust must name the **edge's\n  tunnel IP** — if that's wrong, PROXY headers are ignored or spoofable.\n\n## DNS (public `ai-servicers.com`)\n\n| Record | Value | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| MX | `mail.ai-servicers.com` pri 10 | receivers connect here → Elastic IP |\n| `mail` A | Elastic IP | set in `aws/mail-edge` |\n| PTR | `mail.ai-servicers.com` | **AWS-side**, via the port-25 form — not ours to set |\n| SPF | `v=spf1 mx -all` (or `ip4:<EIP> -all`) | authorise the edge IP as sender |\n| DKIM | generated by DMS (`setup config dkim`) | publish the TXT it emits |\n| DMARC | `v=DMARC1; p=quarantine; rua=mailto:postmaster@ai-servicers.com` | start at `p=none` to monitor |\n\n## Accounts\n\nMailboxes/domains via **postfixadmin** (already in the compose) or `setup email add`. Nothing\nabout account management changes under the edge.\n\n## Test plan (before trusting it)\n\n1. **Tunnel up:** `wg show` both ends; ping tunnel IPs.\n2. **Receive:** from an external account, mail to a test mailbox; confirm delivery.\n3. **Real IP preserved:** check `Received:` headers + Rspamd logs show the *sender's* IP, not\n   the edge tunnel IP. This is the whole point — if it shows the tunnel IP, PROXY protocol is\n   misconfigured.\n4. **Send:** `swaks --to you@gmail.com --from test@ai-servicers.com --server <tunnel>` ; confirm\n   it leaves via the edge (outbound 25 must be unblocked first) and lands in inbox, not spam.\n5. **Deliverability:** mail-tester.com / check SPF+DKIM+DMARC all pass, PTR matches (`dig -x`).\n6. **Fail2ban:** confirm it bans on the real client IP, not the tunnel.\n\n## Current stack state (2026-07-09)\n\n- `mailserver` + `postfixadmin` containers are **defined but not running** (not in `docker ps -a`).\n- Traefik currently holds 25/465/587/993 on the host. Under this design those move to the AWS\n  edge / WireGuard path — **decide** whether Traefik keeps any mail port locally or steps out.\n- No PROXY-protocol config present yet.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Docker Mailserver — Mail Server behind a Proxy][dmsproxy]\n- [DMS issue #3866 — PROXY protocol via env (future simplification)][iss]\n\n[dmsproxy]: https://docker-mailserver.github.io/docker-mailserver/edge/examples/tutorials/mailserver-behind-proxy/\n[iss]: https://github.com/docker-mailserver/docker-mailserver/issues/3866\n","numLines":106,"startLine":1,"totalLines":106}}}
