{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NYczKYykNXn8WTR5RxzbwH","type":"tool_result","content":"195\t## Known Issues & Limitations\n196\t\n197\t### 🔴 CRITICAL: Incoming Mail Blocked by ISP\n198\t**Problem**: Verizon (and most residential ISPs) block incoming port 25\n199\t**Impact**: Cannot receive external email (Gmail, etc.)\n200\t**Current Workaround**: None - incoming mail does not work\n201\t\n202\t**Status of Email Functions:**\n203\t- ✅ **Sending mail**: Works via SendGrid relay\n204\t- ✅ **Internal mail**: Between local users works\n205\t- ✅ **IMAP access**: Nextcloud can read local mail\n206\t- ❌ **Receiving external mail**: BLOCKED by ISP\n207\t\n208\t### Port 25 Workaround Solutions\n209\t\n210\t#### Option 1: AWS SES + Lambda (Recommended)\n211\t**Full implementation plan available**: `/home/administrator/projects/AINotes/PORT25-WORKAROUND.md`\n212\t\n213\t**How it works:**\n214\t1. AWS SES receives mail on port 25 (in AWS cloud)\n215\t2. Lambda function forwards to home server on port 2525\n216\t3. Docker-Mailserver accepts forwarded mail\n217\t4. Nextcloud Mail shows received emails\n218\t\n219\t**Cost**: ~$1-2/month\n220\t**Complexity**: Medium\n221\t**Benefits**: Full control, no Gmail dependency\n222\t\n223\t#### Option 2: VPS Mail Relay\n224\t- Rent VPS from DigitalOcean/Vultr ($6/month)\n225\t- Run mail relay on VPS\n226\t- Forward to home on alternate port\n227\t\n228\t#### Option 3: Cloudflare Email Routing (Free)\n229\t- Forward to Gmail/other email provider\n230\t- Loses independence goal\n231\t- But free and works immediately\n232\t\n233\t### Why Port 25 is Blocked\n234\t- ISPs block to prevent spam from residential connections\n235\t- Cannot be bypassed with port forwarding\n236\t- Email protocol requires port 25 for receiving\n237\t- No alternative ports for incoming SMTP\n238\t\n239\t## Troubleshooting"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4887fea5-78a1-4b14-a071-ae362ca71a13","uuid":"9f5f907f-c19d-43c1-831f-ae0c9ac048c4","timestamp":"2026-07-28T13:55:57.294Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/CLAUDE.md","content":"## Known Issues & Limitations\n\n### 🔴 CRITICAL: Incoming Mail Blocked by ISP\n**Problem**: Verizon (and most residential ISPs) block incoming port 25\n**Impact**: Cannot receive external email (Gmail, etc.)\n**Current Workaround**: None - incoming mail does not work\n\n**Status of Email Functions:**\n- ✅ **Sending mail**: Works via SendGrid relay\n- ✅ **Internal mail**: Between local users works\n- ✅ **IMAP access**: Nextcloud can read local mail\n- ❌ **Receiving external mail**: BLOCKED by ISP\n\n### Port 25 Workaround Solutions\n\n#### Option 1: AWS SES + Lambda (Recommended)\n**Full implementation plan available**: `/home/administrator/projects/AINotes/PORT25-WORKAROUND.md`\n\n**How it works:**\n1. AWS SES receives mail on port 25 (in AWS cloud)\n2. Lambda function forwards to home server on port 2525\n3. Docker-Mailserver accepts forwarded mail\n4. Nextcloud Mail shows received emails\n\n**Cost**: ~$1-2/month\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Benefits**: Full control, no Gmail dependency\n\n#### Option 2: VPS Mail Relay\n- Rent VPS from DigitalOcean/Vultr ($6/month)\n- Run mail relay on VPS\n- Forward to home on alternate port\n\n#### Option 3: Cloudflare Email Routing (Free)\n- Forward to Gmail/other email provider\n- Loses independence goal\n- But free and works immediately\n\n### Why Port 25 is Blocked\n- ISPs block to prevent spam from residential connections\n- Cannot be bypassed with port forwarding\n- Email protocol requires port 25 for receiving\n- No alternative ports for incoming SMTP\n\n## Troubleshooting","numLines":45,"startLine":195,"totalLines":271}}}
